                                "sense_id": "2b0a334b-9c01-30db-a7dc-5c5ff25d564b",
                                "text": "M. Vien, secretary of the college of medicine, published a very complete Loimology."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d6ebc6f-fe17-4f31-834f-5a0b6b37aeb3",
                                "sense_id": "2b0a334b-9c01-30db-a7dc-5c5ff25d564b",
                                "text": "The loimology of the future had for its object to discover what places and what times were favorable to each epidemic disease and what unfavorable, either continuously or for a time […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "80ba1095-8320-4f1d-b7d2-1a14cccb1c67",
                                "sense_id": "2b0a334b-9c01-30db-a7dc-5c5ff25d564b",
                                "text": "Zeiss also elaborated on the connections between the collection of live cultures and his own epidemiological theories, especially his notions of geomedicine and loimology."
                            }
                        ]
